    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the `frai` CLI where the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through to the `frai-gate` subcommand.\n\n### The Problem\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag wasn't reaching the underlying `frai-gate` CLI. The issue was in how the `gate` command handler passed arguments to the spawned `frai-gate` process. The action handler was only receiving positional arguments (`args` parameter), not the command-line flags.\n\n### The Solution\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 742-755) to:\n1. Extract all raw command-line arguments after the `gate` command using `process.argv`\n2. Pass all arguments (including flags like `--ci`) to the spawned `frai-gate` CLI\n\nThe key changes:\n- Changed the action handler to use `process.argv.indexOf('gate')` to find the gate command position\n- Extract all subsequent arguments with `process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1)`\n- Pass the complete argument list to `spawnSync` instead of just positional args\n\n### Verification\n\u2705 **With `--ci` flag**: Creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\u2705 **Without `--ci` flag**: Creates only `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n\u2705 **Rebuilt successfully** with `pnpm --filter frai build`",
